      "content": "That sounds like a great start. I like the name Dark Ferghana Steppes. Since they're supposed to be the main threat to my empire, can you go deeper into how their \"wild\" and \"primitive\" nature actually manifests in their behavior? Like, how does their lack of the empire's \"civilized\" morality or laws make them more terrifying for my protagonists to deal with? I want to make sure the reader really feels the clash between their untamed way of life and the empire's sophisticated culture.",
